{"summary":"Use zero fill between 128-bit integer output chunks","explanation":"Both `Uint128.OStreamValueTest` and `Int128.OStreamValueTest` fail in `os.str() == test_case.expected` for multi-chunk octal and hexadecimal values. For example, with octal formatting, `os.str()` is `"1                    0"` while `test_case.expected` is `"1000000000000000000000"`; with hexadecimal formatting, `os.str()` is `"8              0"` while `test_case.expected` is `"8000000000000000"`. The formatter pads lower chunks with spaces in both its high-chunk and mid-chunk branches, splitting the digits. Zero fill preserves each chunk’s width and makes the digit sequence contiguous for both signed and unsigned output.","edits":[{"path":"absl/numeric/int128.cc","old":"  if (Uint128Low64(high) != 0) {
    os << Uint128Low64(high);
    os << std::noshowbase << std::setfill(' ') << std::setw(div_base_log);
    os << Uint128Low64(mid);","new":"  if (Uint128Low64(high) != 0) {
    os << Uint128Low64(high);
    os << std::noshowbase << std::setfill('0') << std::setw(div_base_log);
    os << Uint128Low64(mid);"},{"path":"absl/numeric/int128.cc","old":"  } else if (Uint128Low64(mid) != 0) {
    os << Uint128Low64(mid);
    os << std::noshowbase << std::setfill(' ') << std::setw(div_base_log);
  }","new":"  } else if (Uint128Low64(mid) != 0) {
    os << Uint128Low64(mid);
    os << std::noshowbase << std::setfill('0') << std::setw(div_base_log);
  }"}]}
